# Line-ending policy for files a Linux container consumes VERBATIM.
#
# A default Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) materializes these with
# CRLF, which breaks the community self-host build in ways CI never sees
# (CI and Railway check out with LF):
#   - The Dockerfile's embedded heredoc scripts (install-pinned-ffmpeg.sh,
#     start.sh) run under dash inside the container: "set: pipefail:
#     invalid option name" kills the image build at the runner stage
#     (clean-machine matrix finding, 2026-08-11, Windows).
#   - docker/selfhost/roles.sql is volume-mounted into Postgres first-init
#     and read by psql, whose backtick \set line must not carry \r.
#
# Deliberately targeted, not a blanket `* text=auto` — a repo-wide
# renormalization would touch thousands of files for no benefit.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
docker/** text eol=lf
frontend/Caddyfile text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
